-- title:
--   Ramification over the j(q^N)-line for a good model
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be an algebraically closed field, $N\ge 1$ a natural number with $N\neq 0$ in $K$, and $j_0\in K$. Let $M$ be a field extension of $K$ containing an element $t$ transcendental over $K$ with $M$ finite-dimensional over $K\langle t\rangle$, and let $W_0$ be a place of $M$ over $K$, that is, a valuation subring of $M$, not equal to $M$, containing $\operatorname{im}(K\to M)$ and a principal ideal ring; write $\kappa$ for its residue field and $\operatorname{ord}_{W_0}$ for minus the logarithm of the associated $\mathbb{Z}^{m0}$-valued adic valuation. Assume $\operatorname{ord}_{W_0}(t-j_0)>0$. Let $W$ be a Weierstrass curve over the valuation ring of $W_0$ whose reduction $\overline W$ modulo the maximal ideal has $\Delta\neq 0$, whose base change $W_M$ to $M$ has $\Delta\neq 0$, and with $j(W_M)=t$. Let $Q$ be a point of the affine curve $W_M$ of exact additive order $N$ such that the Vélu full-kernel quotient $W_M/\langle Q\rangle$, formed by `fullKernelQuotient` from the sums of $\mathrm{g}^x$ and $x\mathrm{g}^x-y\mathrm{g}^y$ over the odd-order summing set of $Q$, again has $\Delta\neq 0$. Let $\psi$ be a $K$-algebra homomorphism from `modularFunctionFieldFullC K N`, the subfield of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,K$ generated over $K$ by the series $q\mapsto q^d$ substituted into the $q$-expansion $j(q)$ for the divisors $d\mid N$, into $M$, sending $j(q)$ to $t$ and $j(q^N)$ to $j(W_M/\langle Q\rangle)$. Finally let $j_0'\in K$ satisfy $\operatorname{ord}_{W_0}(\psi(j(q^N))-j_0')>0$. Then, as an identity in $\mathbb{Z}$, $\operatorname{ord}_{W_0}(\psi(j(q^N))-j_0')$ times the number of variable changes $\gamma$ over $\kappa$ with $\gamma\cdot\overline W=\overline W$ which preserve the cyclic subgroup generated by the reduction $\overline Q$ of $Q$ (each $T$ in that subgroup has its image under $\gamma$'s inverse point map `Point.vcInvFun` equal, as a heterogeneous equality, to some $T'$ in the subgroup) equals the ramification index of $W_0$ along $\psi$ — the least $n>0$ of the form $\operatorname{ord}_{W_0}(\psi f)$ for $f\neq 0$ in the modular function field — times the cardinality of the stabiliser of $\overline W/\langle\overline Q\rangle$ in the group of variable changes over $\kappa$.
--
--   This is the companion, read over the $j(q^N)$-line, of the ramification identity $\operatorname{ord}_{W_0}(t-j_0)\cdot\#\mathrm{Stab}=e\cdot\#\mathrm{Aut}(\overline W)$ over the $j$-line, in the style of Igusa's comparison of ramification on modular curves with automorphisms of the reduced curve and its Vélu quotient. It feeds the construction of equivariant torsion reductions used to evaluate $j$ of the full-kernel quotient at a place.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_ord_sub_mul_natCard_stabilizer_zmultiples_reduceHom_eq_ramificationIndexAlong_mul_natCard_stabilizer_fullKernelQuotient.lean

